{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fe546ad04bc45c7bf0bd5abb30cd019b70557b084646fb92d1b45ff7975e2c20","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar-brainstorm skill documentation","key_entities":["examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md","rebar review-plan --force","rebar ready","plan-review gate","claimability fast-fail"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","blocked tickets","plan-review gate","force flag","policy enforcement","agent guidance"],"propositions":["Blocked or not-yet-claimable tickets represent a successful terminal state of the current review cycle and require no further agent action until dependencies resolve.","The --force flag to rebar review-plan is reserved for human operators only; agents must not use it to bypass the claimability fast-fail based on vague or implied instructions.","Agents encountering ambiguous instructions about forced reviews should ask a single clarifying question naming the block and risk rather than inferring authorization to force.","Forced reviews create signed attestations against non-final dependencies that can silently become stale; repeated individual force attempts collectively defeat the gate's intended safety mechanism."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787731119371116001,"uuid":"7ac94d48-0274-40e0-bf26-f3fb6e0986f4"}